# s17_composite.tkr — §17 composite predicate `#if(os == "linux" && arch == "x86_64")`. The arm
# survives only when BOTH axes match; an #else provides the fallback. On the linux/x86_64 host the
# conjunction holds and `pick` returns 99.

Feature: §17 composite predicate — a conjunction selects the arm only on the matching os+arch pair

  Scenario: linux_x86_64_pair — on linux/x86_64 the conjunction arm returns 99
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 99
